From: genetixteam <genetixteam@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:24:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: resolve eth0.X down to eth0 for the hw flowtable

Take the v1 EX20v port's fw4 patch. netifd reports no devtype for the
econet eth0.X 8021q devices, so fw4 put eth0.1/eth0.35 in the flowtable
instead of eth0. nft_dev_forward_path() needs the fully resolved lower
device in the flowtable; without it every flow stays XMIT_NEIGH, the
REDIRECT target is the VLAN device and econet-eth refuses the offload
(repl_rej_odev), so all routed traffic goes through the CPU.

Fall back to DEVTYPE from sysfs uevent when netifd has none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YbeF2izcaoFj6qx1YBoB3j
